# Interpreter-throw closure item 3 (steps/interpreter-throw-20261010.md): a walker fault while evaluating a CALL'S
# ACTUAL -- `twice(12 / n)` with n = 0 -- is the walked caller's own interpreter throw (a throw from an actual remains
# that throw; the callee never runs) and the caller's handler takes it.  Exit 7; 24 would mean twice ran.
fn: twice (int: x) int
    return: x + x

fn: relay (int: n) int
    int: got 0
    ---
        got: twice(12 / n)
    ---
    catch: interpreter ()
        got: 7
return: got

int: result relay(0)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
